<title>NEW ZEALAND: ANZ cuts 3-year fixed mortgage rate to 8.95 pct.</title>
<headline>ANZ cuts 3-year fixed mortgage rate to 8.95 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANZ and PostBank on Friday said they were cutting their three-year fixed mortgage rate to 8.95 percent from 9.25 percent to reflect lower long-term wholesale interest rates.</p>
<p>The new rate is effective from Monday.</p>
<p>AMP phone banking subsidiary Ergo earlier said it was cutting its three-year fixed rate to 8.9 percent from 9.5 percent. -- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
